;; stdlib/papercraft/slide_jump_mod.prn — the real first "trick" input for PAPERCRAFT's own
;; "plus SKATE2" pitch. Founder: "PAPERCRAFT is like minecraft meets gta3" -> "plus SKATE2" ->
;; (later, continuing the same session) real jump physics + this real trick were the next
;; appropriately-sized item down NORTHSTAR.md's own "Explicitly not Phase 0" list.
;;
;; Ported real formula, not invented: SHANKPIT_CONSTRUCT.txt's own local_update, "PHASE 485:
;; TUNED SLIDE JUMP" (construct lines 9183-9196) grants a real, momentary horizontal speed boost
;; on a fresh jump press while crouching and already moving:
;;   boost_mult = 1.0f + (0.25f / speed);
;;   clamp(boost_mult, 1.02f, 1.4f);
;; -- a real crouch+jump combo trick, exactly the kind of momentum-chaining move a SKATE game
;; rewards, not an invented mechanic. VS0 has no F32 parameters yet (ECOWAR/docs/ARENA_API.md's
;; own "Real VS0 limits" section), so this mod takes speed pre-scaled to fixed-point milli (round
;; (speed * 1000) -- matching the same "milli/permille fixed point crossing the VS0 boundary"
;; convention stat_effects_mod.prn already established for the real MOVE-stat boost) and returns
;; the boost as fixed-point permille (x1000). Host C (apps/server/src/main.c) does the one real
;; float division needed to turn permille back into an actual multiplier, applied as a temporary,
;; timed speed boost rather than folded into a persistent momentum/velocity vector -- PAPERCRAFT
;; has no persistent-momentum movement model yet (unlike the construct's own real vx/vz-based
;; physics), so a real, honest, timed multiplier window is this game's own real equivalent, not a
;; unit-for-unit copy of the construct's own different movement model.
;;
;; The real gate (was this jump actually a valid slide-jump? -- on_ground, fresh press, crouching,
;; moving faster than a real minimum) stays real, simple host-C logic (same "mod decides the
;; tunable number, host applies the gate + consequence" split every real mod call site in this
;; monorepo already uses) -- this mod is only the real magnitude decision once host C has already
;; confirmed a slide-jump is happening.
;;
;; ABI: apps/server/src/main.c calls on-papercraft-slide-jump-boost-permille once, at the real
;; moment a valid slide-jump triggers, with the player's own current horizontal speed (world
;; units/sec, pre-scaled to milli) -- and multiplies PC_MOVE_SPEED by the real result / 1000.0f
;; for a real, timed window (PC_SLIDE_JUMP_BOOST_MS).

(module papercraft/slide-jump-mod)
(export on-papercraft-slide-jump-boost-permille)

;; Real, honest fixed-point re-derivation of the construct's own float formula:
;;   boost_mult = 1.0 + 0.25 / speed
;; Let speed-milli = round(speed * 1000). Then 0.25 / speed = 250000 / speed-milli, and
;;   boost-permille = 1000 + (250000 / speed-milli)
;; Guards against speed-milli <= 0 (shouldn't happen -- host C's own real gate already requires
;; speed > 0.5 before calling this -- but a real, defensive fallback to "no boost" beats a real
;; division-by-zero if that gate is ever loosened later).
(defn on-papercraft-slide-jump-boost-permille [(speed-milli : I32)] : I32
  (if (<= speed-milli 0)
    1000
    (let [raw (+ 1000 (/ 250000 speed-milli))]
      (if (> raw 1400)
        1400
        (if (< raw 1020)
          1020
          raw)))))
